{"id":"d41695b9af12c800","group":"58","path":"58/batch02/58-df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence.md","title":"ZFC Measure7 Kl Divergence","display":"df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence — ZFC Measure7 Kl Divergence","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence","aliases":["58-df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence"],"display":"df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence — ZFC Measure7 Kl Divergence","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-probability.md]]","[[58-df-integral]]","[[58-df-radon-nikodym]]","[[../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence — ZFC Measure7 Kl Divergence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5e0db065132180df\" href=\"?note=5e0db065132180df\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-probability.md\">../batch08/58-df-probability.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"58-df-integral\">58-df-integral</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"31e71a3e39e9a1b8\" href=\"?note=31e71a3e39e9a1b8\" title=\"58-df-radon-nikodym\">58-df-radon-nikodym</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md\">../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\mathcal A,\\mu,\\nu,r,f,g\\in V\">\\(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu,\\nu,r,f,g\\in V\\)</span> (measurable space, probabilities, divergence, density, and nonnegative integrand)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7KlDivergence}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7KlDivergence}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\">\\(\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\)</span> (sigma-algebra predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}\\)</span> (probability-measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"5e0db065132180df\" href=\"?note=5e0db065132180df\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-probability.md\">../batch08/58-df-probability.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)\">\\(\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)\\)</span> means that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f=d\\mu/d\\nu\">\\(f=d\\mu/d\\nu\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"31e71a3e39e9a1b8\" href=\"?note=31e71a3e39e9a1b8\" title=\"58-df-radon-nikodym\">58-df-radon-nikodym</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_+\">\\(\\mathcal B_+\\)</span> is the Borel sigma algebra of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[0,\\infty]\">\\([0,\\infty]\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> is the measurable-function predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> is the set-function predicate, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int_X\\cdot\\,d\\nu\">\\(\\int_X\\cdot\\,d\\nu\\)</span> is the nonnegative integral (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"58-df-integral\">58-df-integral</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure7\\text{-}kl\\text{-}divergence} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7KlDivergence}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu,\\nu,r)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left(\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal A,X)\\land\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mu,X,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\nu,X,\\mathcal A)\\land\nr\\in[0,\\infty]\\land\n\\Bigl(\n\\bigl[\n\\exists f,g\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(g,X,[0,\\infty])\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal A),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\\land\n\\forall x\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\n(f(x)=0\\to g(x)=1)\\land\n(0&lt;f(x)&lt;+\\infty\\to g(x)=f(x)\\log f(x)-f(x)+1)\\land\n(f(x)=+\\infty\\to g(x)=+\\infty)\n\\Bigr)\\land r=\\int_X g\\,d\\nu\n\\Bigr)\n\\bigr]\\lor\n\\bigl[\n\\exists A\\in\\mathcal A\\;(\\nu(A)=0\\land\\mu(A)&gt;0)\\land r=+\\infty\n\\bigr]\n\\Bigr)\n\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure7\\text{-}kl\\text{-}divergence} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7KlDivergence}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu,\\nu,r)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left(\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal A,X)\\land\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mu,X,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\nu,X,\\mathcal A)\\land\nr\\in[0,\\infty]\\land\n\\Bigl(\n\\bigl[\n\\exists f,g\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(g,X,[0,\\infty])\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal A),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\\land\n\\forall x\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\n(f(x)=0\\to g(x)=1)\\land\n(0&lt;f(x)&lt;+\\infty\\to g(x)=f(x)\\log f(x)-f(x)+1)\\land\n(f(x)=+\\infty\\to g(x)=+\\infty)\n\\Bigr)\\land r=\\int_X g\\,d\\nu\n\\Bigr)\n\\bigr]\\lor\n\\bigl[\n\\exists A\\in\\mathcal A\\;(\\nu(A)=0\\land\\mu(A)&gt;0)\\land r=+\\infty\n\\bigr]\n\\Bigr)\n\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>In the absolutely continuous case, the upstream signature is called as <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)\">\\(\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)\\)</span>, whose meaning is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f=d\\mu/d\\nu\">\\(f=d\\mu/d\\nu\\)</span>.  For probability measures,\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int(f\\log f-f+1)\\,d\\nu=\\int\\log(f)\\,d\\mu\">\\(\\int(f\\log f-f+1)\\,d\\nu=\\int\\log(f)\\,d\\mu\\)</span>; the former integrand is nonnegative and therefore lies in the domain of the registered nonnegative Lebesgue integral.  The displayed cases fix the conventions at <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0\">\\(0\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+\\infty\">\\(+\\infty\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md","status":"resolved","id":"a740bdad87b97ac6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-probability.md","status":"resolved","id":"5e0db065132180df","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-probability.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-integral","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-integral]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-radon-nikodym","status":"resolved","id":"31e71a3e39e9a1b8","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-radon-nikodym]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md","status":"resolved","id":"a740bdad87b97ac6","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}$ (sigma-algebra predicate, see [[../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-probability.md","status":"resolved","id":"5e0db065132180df","anchor":"ref-9","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}$ (probability-measure predicate, see [[../batch08/58-df-probability.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-radon-nikodym","status":"resolved","id":"31e71a3e39e9a1b8","anchor":"ref-10","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)$ means that $f=d\\mu/d\\nu$ (see [[58-df-radon-nikodym]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-integral","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-11","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}$ is the set-function predicate, and $\\int_X\\cdot\\,d\\nu$ is the nonnegative integral (see [[58-df-integral]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,\\mathcal A,\\mu,\\nu,r,f,g\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7KlDivergence}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)","display":false},{"tex":"f=d\\mu/d\\nu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B_+","display":false},{"tex":"[0,\\infty]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\int_X\\cdot\\,d\\nu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure7\\text{-}kl\\text{-}divergence} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7KlDivergence}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu,\\nu,r)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left(\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal A,X)\\land\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mu,X,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\nu,X,\\mathcal A)\\land\nr\\in[0,\\infty]\\land\n\\Bigl(\n\\bigl[\n\\exists f,g\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(g,X,[0,\\infty])\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal A),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\\land\n\\forall x\\in X\\;\\Bigl(\n(f(x)=0\\to g(x)=1)\\land\n(0<f(x)<+\\infty\\to g(x)=f(x)\\log f(x)-f(x)+1)\\land\n(f(x)=+\\infty\\to g(x)=+\\infty)\n\\Bigr)\\land r=\\int_X g\\,d\\nu\n\\Bigr)\n\\bigr]\\lor\n\\bigl[\n\\exists A\\in\\mathcal A\\;(\\nu(A)=0\\land\\mu(A)>0)\\land r=+\\infty\n\\bigr]\n\\Bigr)\n\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RNDerivative}_S(f,\\mu,\\nu;X,\\mathcal A)","display":false},{"tex":"f=d\\mu/d\\nu","display":false},{"tex":"\\int(f\\log f-f+1)\\,d\\nu=\\int\\log(f)\\,d\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"0","display":false},{"tex":"+\\infty","display":false}],"bytes":2561,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-2634","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence.md|58-df-zfc-measure7-kl-divergence]]（batch02）"}],"outgoing":["a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","a740bdad87b97ac6","5e0db065132180df","4884f45058a56aac","31e71a3e39e9a1b8","bbbec05fde1d3b01","36d7463d215be751"]}